{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The impossibility boundary is too restrictive: it assumes the only graph-enrichment vector is monotone edge construction, but a non-monotone enrichment (e.g., contracting a strongly-connected defense cycle into a single macro-node) can strictly increase the accepted set while preserving determinism, polynomial cost, and committed-root validity, thereby falsifying the claim that vocabulary enrichment is the only responsible strengthening.","target":"03b83a832db51e34f2fbaf9ba35d94f4d24a45d07052ce38db24031120f1d031"},{"attack":true,"case":"The shortest-defense-path requirement breaks reinstatement as a derived property: an argument A reinstated by B (where B defends A) may be assigned a shorter witness-minimal path through an unrelated attacker C whose shortest path to a committed root is shorter than the path through B, so the oracle can reject A's reinstatement even though B is the genuine defender — meaning reinstatement is no longer derived from the grounded extension but is overridden by the canonical path ordering.","target":"82337d08a1c77dab7f79b215bf03307040b600fcfe1537297d0a1a9a5514f746"}]}